@base = http://localhost:5080

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Infer a mapping from one A/B example
POST {{base}}/api/mappings/infer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "people-v2",
  "save": true,
  "source": { "first": "Jane", "last": "Doe", "mail": " JANE@X.COM ", "age": "34" },
  "target": { "name": "Jane Doe", "contact": { "email": "jane@x.com" }, "age": 34 }
}

### Transform a record with the saved mapping
POST {{base}}/api/transform
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mappingName": "people-v2",
  "input": { "first": "Sam", "last": "Lee", "mail": "SAM@Y.COM", "age": "41" }
}

### Dry-run a migration from a file in the data folder
POST {{base}}/api/migrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mappingName": "people-v2",
  "source": { "type": "file", "path": "people.json" },
  "dryRun": true
}

### Real migration: file -> ndjson, with dead letters
POST {{base}}/api/migrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mappingName": "people-v2",
  "source": { "type": "file", "path": "people.json" },
  "sink": { "type": "file", "path": "out/people-v2.ndjson" },
  "deadLetterPath": "out/people-failed.ndjson",
  "batchSize": 1000,
  "maxErrors": 50
}

### Migration: HTTP API -> HTTP API
POST {{base}}/api/migrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mappingName": "people-v2",
  "source": { "type": "http", "url": "http://localhost:9000/legacy/people", "recordsPath": "$.data" },
  "sink": { "type": "http", "url": "http://localhost:9001/v2/people/bulk", "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer xyz" } },
  "batchSize": 200
}

### List migrations
GET {{base}}/api/migrations

### MCP: list tools
POST {{base}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list" }
